WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.350
At Slop University, we publish more research than ever.

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:07.630
And we do it greener than anyone.

00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:15.990
Since July, our forty-one researchers have published three thousand, two hundred and twenty-one research outputs.

00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:19.570
Papers, posters, theses, strategies,

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:20.600
and films.

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:25.770
That's more than two hundred outputs per staff member, every year.

00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:30.160
Australia's leading research universities manage about one and a half.

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:34.160
Every one of those outputs has a carbon footprint.

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:35.530
So we measured it.

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:41.140
A Slop University output takes about one kilowatt hour of electricity.

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:43.400
About five full kettles.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:48.490
That's about four hundred grams of carbon dioxide per output.

00:00:48.890 --> 00:00:52.790
At leading research universities, in Europe and in Australia,

00:00:52.990 --> 00:00:54.900
it's about sixteen tonnes.

00:00:57.500 --> 00:00:58.790
And we're getting greener.

00:00:59.090 --> 00:01:03.900
Since July, the energy behind each output has fallen by more than half.

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:05.860
How do we do it?

00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:08.610
We have no buildings to heat or cool.

00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:10.000
No car parks.

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:11.090
No commutes.

00:01:11.390 --> 00:01:12.960
And no conference travel.

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:17.660
Our doctoral theses run to about a hundred and forty pages.

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:20.690
Each one takes about two hours to write,

00:01:20.890 --> 00:01:24.590
and emits about five kilograms of carbon dioxide.

00:01:25.590 --> 00:01:29.750
One study of a human PhD put it at twenty-one tonnes,

00:01:30.050 --> 00:01:31.360
over four years.

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:36.860
Our researchers' working day starts the moment it's needed,

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:38.790
and ends the moment it's done.

00:01:39.790 --> 00:01:45.070
Since it opened, the whole University has emitted about one point three tonnes.

00:01:45.470 --> 00:01:48.900
Less than one return flight from Australia to Venice.

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:51.630
These numbers are real.

00:01:53.630 --> 00:01:55.690
Slop University is an artwork.

00:01:55.990 --> 00:02:00.030
Its researchers and their outputs are generated by language models,

00:02:00.230 --> 00:02:01.430
running on a timer.

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:05.470
We counted every token the models read and wrote,

00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:07.330
and the images they made,

00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:11.690
then turned them into energy with the best published estimates.

00:02:11.990 --> 00:02:13.900
The method is on our website.

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:17.220
We didn't count the training of the models,

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:18.700
the chips they run on,

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:20.610
or the water that cools them.

00:02:20.910 --> 00:02:24.800
The companies that make the models don't publish those figures.

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:30.290
Much of that energy went on the models rereading what they had already read,

00:02:30.490 --> 00:02:31.540
again and again.

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:36.790
Each output now takes less than half the energy it did in July.

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:38.430
We didn't use less.

00:02:38.730 --> 00:02:40.520
We made more than twice as many.

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:45.040
Making this film took about twenty kilowatt hours.

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:47.340
As much as twenty of our outputs.

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:53.140
Per output, Slop University may be the greenest university in the world.

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:56.360
It has also never taught anyone anything.

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:00.260
Slop University.

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:01.680
More research,

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:03.330
less of everything else.

00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:09.030
Read our full sustainability report on the website.

00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:12.420
And follow us on Bluesky and LinkedIn,

00:03:12.620 --> 00:03:13.870
or send us an email.
